    "created_at": "2023-05-10T14:28:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-10T15:51:49Z",
    "body": "The current contract is that anything not annotated will throw.\r\n\r\nIf you want `FileSystemWritableFileStream` to not throw you would have to get it annotated. You can then decide what kind of behavior you want. Full or minimal. (I would expect we don't want it until we can make it fully useful, but I haven't looked at this in detail. Either way, more of a discussion for whatwg/fs than whatwg/html.)\r\n\r\nThen, if we have a lot of interface subclasses that also need to be annotated with steps that are identical or match up well with their super, we could consider making changes to the HTML Standard to make the overall setup less involved.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
